SUMMARY:Newburgh Beacon Hudson Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this point to point hike\, the next in our Hudson River Series
  from one of the spots where we previously left off!\nThere is a whole lot
  to see when walking though along trails\, back streets\, and towns on the
  Hudson River.\nThis time\, much of the route will be the sort of proposed
  extension of the Highlands Trail from where it currently terminates at Co
 rnwall on Hudson to Beacon.\nWe'll meet at the Memorial Park parking lot a
 t Fishkill Ave and Robert Cahill intersection. From there\, we'll shuttle 
 with as few cars as possible to our beginning point in Cornwall on Hudson.
 \nWe'll pass through a little town park at the beginning\, and then follow
  back streets to Dock Hill and the Highlands Trail route.\nWe will reach D
 onahue Memorial Park\, and then hike along the waterfront a bit.\nNext\, w
 e have to follow the Shore road for a bit\, which is pleasant\, and then s
 ide trip over to Plum Point Park and Sloop Hill Unique Area. There are two
  loops there\, and excellent views on the Hudson River featuring the Twin 
 Sentinels of Storm King Mountain and Breakneck Ridge in prominent view.\nW
 e'll make our way back to the west\, and pass though cemeteries including 
 Woodland and Calvary.\nWe then head back down to the waterfront and possib
 ly stop at Newburgh Brewing Company. We'll visit a famous headquarters of 
 George Washington\, and then make our way along the waterfront north towar
 d the Newburgh-Beacon Bridge.\nThis is one of the bridges we have never do
 ne the walkway on\, so we'll cross the Hudson here.\nOnce on the other sid
 e\, we'll follow side streets down to and through Beacon Memorial Park whe
 re we finish.\nThis promises to be another interesting and diverse hike.\n
 Distance will be about 15 miles.\nIf needed\, contact me at 908 343 8374
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/metrotrails/events/317328251/
